      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona 23 Aug 2026 – Cardrona picked up 10-15 cm of fresh snow overnight, but with gale-force winds gusting to 137 km/h and a deteriorating forecast, the mountain is closed for the day. It's a cold -5°C up at the 1800m weather station, where the natural base now sits at 60 cm. All ten lifts are closed, including the Whitestar Express, Captains Express and McDougall's Chondola, along with every terrain park and marked run on the mountain. Ride Tribe, Mini and Academy programs have all been cancelled for today. Access roads are open but chains are required across the board — 2WD vehicles need to chain up from Heli Corner, and 4WD from Valley View, with an active road hazard advisory in place. The team will try again tomorrow; anyone needing to adjust a booking can reach out to the Cardrona team directly.",
