      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 23 Aug 2026 – Storm riders, this one's for you — Treble Cone has picked up 15cm-plus of fresh snow overnight at the top of the six-seater, and it's still falling. A brief clearance gave way to the storm rolling back in, so visibility has dropped, but the skiing underfoot is excellent with fresh snow filling in yesterday's tracks. It's -4°C with wind gusting to 103 km/h. The Home Basin Express and Beginner Platter are running, opening up Home Basin, Matukituki Basin and Powder Bowl, all skiing well despite the reduced visibility. The Saddle Quad and Saddle Basin are closed for the day — it's simply too wild up there. Grooming is limited given the conditions, though Triple Treat and Main Street have both been groomed. Touring and skinning access is closed today, and Ride Tribe has been postponed. All vehicles need to carry chains on the way up, or better yet, carpool or catch the free road shuttle — the road is very wet and muddy, with an active hazard advisory in place. Rug up, keep an eye on the wind holds, and get amongst it.",
